flowchart TD
    A[Create or activate conda env] --> B[Install matching requirements file]
    B --> C[`python train.py`]
    C --> D[Hydra loads `config/config1.yaml`]

    D --> E[Build qCLEVR dataloaders]
    E --> E1[Each sample yields cue image, mixture image, target count]

    D --> F[Instantiate `Conv2dEIRNN`]
    F --> F1[4 recurrent conv EI layers]
    F --> F2[5 recurrent steps per stimulus]
    F --> F3[Low-rank cue modulation on layer outputs]
    F --> F4[Feedback path: L2->L1, L3->L2, L4->L3]

    E1 --> G[Training loop]
    F --> G
    G --> H[Cue pass primes hidden states]
    H --> I[Mixture pass reuses cue context]

    I --> J[Per layer and timestep: excitatory update]
    J --> K[Interneuron inhibition and Euler state update]
    K --> L[Average pooling produces next layer input]
    L --> M[Apply cue-driven low-rank modulation]
    M --> N[Apply top-down feedback to lower layers]

    N --> O[Final layer output]
    O --> P[MLP head: Flatten -> Linear -> ReLU -> Dropout -> Linear]
    P --> Q[6-way count logits]
    Q --> R[CrossEntropy loss]
    R --> S[AdamW + OneCycleLR + gradient clipping]
    S --> T[Save checkpoints and training curve PNGs]

    classDef cmd fill:#f5f1e8,stroke:#8a6d3b,color:#2c2416;
    classDef data fill:#e6f4ea,stroke:#2f7a4b,color:#163222;
    classDef model fill:#e8eefc,stroke:#3e63b3,color:#15264b;
    classDef train fill:#f9e8ef,stroke:#b24a72,color:#4b1829;

    class A,B,C cmd;
    class D,E,E1 data;
    class F,F1,F2,F3,F4,H,I,J,K,L,M,N,O,P,Q model;
    class G,R,S,T train;
